Translating IPv4 ----> IPv6

TYPES
Network Address Translation (NAT)   -   Translates private IP addresses to public IP addresses for routing over public networks
    Dynamic NAT (DNAT)
        - Automatically assigns an IP address from a pool and gives a one-to-one translation (like renting out an IP address)
    Static NAT (SNAT) 
        - Manually assigns a public IP address to a private IP address for one-to-one translation (like owning an IP address)
    Port Address Translation (PAT)
        - Sharing of one public IP by multiple private IP addresses which gives a many-to-one translation (like sharing a phone number with extensions)

Different Names of NAT IP Addresses
    Inside Local Address (ILA) - Private IP address assigned to a host on the inside network
    Inside Global Address (IGA) - Public IP address assigned to a host on the inside network
    Outside Local Address (OLA) - Private IP address assigned to a host on the outside network
    Outside Global Address (OGA) - Public IP address assigned to a host on the outside network